+
+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  `soldAt` is an ISO instant with a timezone; `qty` is positive with at most
+  three decimals. Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`, counting new
+  tickets and the sum of their dish quantities. All rows for a previously
+  imported ticket are skipped. Invalid rows (including skipped tickets) and
+  insufficient stock return `bad_request` naming the physical CSV row;
+  row 2 is the first data row. The entire import is atomic.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 2, "actual": 3, "difference": 1 }`.
+  Days are inclusive in UTC; `difference` is actual minus theoretical.
+  Actual includes every consume movement, including sales, dated at soldAt.
+  Results are sorted by item id and omit items with no use.
