+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Migration from schema 2 adds an empty `sales` collection without changing
+  existing records. Each sale row stores `ticket`, `soldAt` (normalized UTC
+  instant), `dishId`, `qty`, and the scaled `ingredients` snapshot.
+- Imported tickets are identified by their exact ticket string. Every row
+  of a new ticket is imported together; previously imported tickets are skipped.
+- Sales consume stock with `ref` `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`. The ingredient
+  snapshot preserves theoretical use if the recipe later changes.
